  "node_log_tail": "hv2-sandboxd: listening on 0.0.0.0:57159, capacity 128\n  POST   /sandboxes                -- E2B-shaped (NewSandbox -> Sandbox), boots a real VM and its own process.Process gRPC listener (port in the response's processPort)\n  POST   /sandboxes/{id}/exec     -- NOT E2B's envd protocol; a real exec_in_guest (simpler than grpcurl-ing processPort)\n  POST   /sandboxes/{id}/connect  -- attach to an existing sandbox; what the E2B SDK's Sandbox.connect() calls\n  DELETE /sandboxes/{id}          -- stop the VM and its process.Process listener\n  PUT    /sandboxes/{id}/network  -- replace a running sandbox's egress rules\n  POST   /sandboxes/{id}/pause    -- suspend to disk; connect or resume brings it back,          and with autoResume so does a request through the proxy\n  POST   /sandboxes/{id}/fork     -- checkpoint in place, start `count` copies\n  GET    /sandboxes/{id}/network/decisions -- NOT E2B's; the gateway's audit log\nsandboxes get no network interface (--network to change that)\nsandboxes are restored from template snapshots: base\n\nsandbox proxy on 0.0.0.0:43863 -- HTTP/2, routed by the authority a client asks for, as 49983-<sandboxID>.<anything>\n  grpcurl -plaintext -authority 49983-$SBX.local -H \"X-Access-Token: $TOKEN\" -import-path crates/hv2-api/proto -proto process.proto \\\n      -d '{\"process\":{\"cmd\":\"/bin/sh\",\"args\":[\"-c\",\"echo hi\"]}}' \\\n      localhost:43863 process.Process/Start\n",
